\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p>Construct a scatter plot that represents this data.</p>\n\n                    </div>     \n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                        <p>We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>First, we draw the independent variable (height) along the horizontal axis.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Then, we draw the dependent variable (weight) along the vertical axis.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This gives us the following scatter plot.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-630817a152951fe1e8bafba13db730ea\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/630817a152951fe1e8bafba13db730ea\"></div> \n\n                    </div>     \n                </div>                            \n                    \n            </div>",
